# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
The purpose of this research plan is to refine and update our understanding of sustainable fashion, with a focus on circular business models. This document builds upon previous research and incorporates new insights gained from The Ordinary&#x27;s skincare products.<br>
<br>
## Circular Business Models<br>
<br>
Our research suggests that successful implementation of circular business models in the fashion industry requires collaboration between designers, manufacturers, and consumers. We propose exploring partnerships with other companies or organizations to develop innovative solutions for sustainable production and consumption.<br>
<br>
## Potential Collaborations<br>
<br>
*   Partnering with textile manufacturers to develop sustainable materials<br>
*   Collaborating with fashion brands to create closed-loop systems for garment production and recycling<br>
*   Exploring opportunities for upcycling or repurposing existing garments<br>
<br>
## Next Steps<br>
<br>
Our next steps will involve further research on successful case studies of circular business models in the fashion industry. We will also explore potential collaborations with other designers, manufacturers, or companies to develop innovative solutions for sustainable production and consumption.<br>
